idden flex items-center justify-center p-3"},["IMG",{"__playwright_current_src__":"http://localhost:3000/images/publications/facing-the-giants-cover.svg","alt":"Facing the Giants","class":"w-full h-full object-contain rounded-md shadow-lg transform group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-300","loading":"lazy","referrerpolicy":"no-referrer","src":"/images/publications/facing-the-giants-cover.svg"}],["DIV",{"class":"absolute top-4 right-4 bg-black/70 backdrop-blur-xs text-amber-300 px-2.5 py-1 rounded text-[10px] font-bold border border-amber-400/40"},"Solo Memoir & Survivor Guide"]],["DIV",{"class":"p-5 flex-1 flex flex-col justify-between space-y-4"},["DIV",{"class":"space-y-1.5"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-[10px] font-bold text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-wider font-mono"},"2021"," Publication"],["H4",{"class":"font-serif text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 group-hover:text-[#104F57] transition-colors"},"Facing the Giants"],["P",{"class":"text-xs text-[#633C69] font-medium"},"A Journey to Freedom from Domestic Abuse"],["P",{"class":"text-xs text-slate-600 line-clamp-3 leading-relaxed pt-1"},"In \"Facing the Giants\", Comfort Dondo recounts her personal journey moving from Zimbabwe to the United States at age 17, surviving childhood trauma and domestic violence, and confronting the towering \"giants\" of systemic isolation, legal intimidation, and cultural silence. The memoir provides a compassionate, practical roadmap for women seeking autonomy, safety, and renewed spiritual faith."]],["DIV",{"class":"pt-2 border-t border-slate-100 flex items-center justify-between"},["BUTTON",{"class":"text-xs font-bold text-[#104F57] hover:text-[#0c3e44] flex items-center gap-1 cursor-pointer"},["SPAN",{},"Read Excerpts & Details"],["svg",{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"24","height":"24","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","stroke-width":"2","stroke-linecap":"round","stroke-linejoin":"round","class":"lucide lucide-chevron-right w-3.5 h-3.5","aria-hidden":"true"},["path",{"d":"m9 18 6-6-6-6"}]]],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[11px] text-slate-400"},"By Comfort Dondo"]]]],["DIV",{"class":"bg-white rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 overflow-hidden shadow-sm hover:shadow-xl transition-all flex flex-col group"},["DIV",{"class":"relative bg-slate-900 aspect-[2/3] overflow-hidden flex items-center justify-center p-3"},["IMG",{"__playwright_current_src__":"http://localhost:3000/images/publications/sacred-promise-cover.svg","alt":"Sacred Promise: An Anthology","class":"w-full h-full object-contain rounded-md shadow-lg transform group-hover:scale-105 transition-transform duration-300","loading":"lazy","referrerpolicy":"no-referrer","src":"/images/publications/sacred-promise-cover.svg"}],["DIV",{"class":"absolute top-4 right-4 bg-black/70 backdrop-blur-xs text-amber-300 px-2.5 py-1 rounded text-[10px] font-bold border border-amber-400/40"},"International Bestseller"]],["DIV",{"class":"p-5 flex-1 flex flex-col justify-between space-y-4"},["DIV",{"class":"space-y-1.5"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-[10px] font-bold text-slate-400 uppercase tracking-wider font-mono"},"2023"," Publication"],["H4",{"class":"font-serif text-lg font-bold text-slate-900 group-hover:text-[#104F57] transition-colors"},"Sacred Promise: An Anthology"],["P",{"class":"text-xs text-[#633C69] font-medium"},"Stories of Resilience and Communal Awakening"],["P",{"class":"text-xs text-slate-600 line-clamp-3 leading-relaxed pt-1"},"Compiled by global educator Dr. Tererai Trent and published by Women Changing the World Press, \"Sacred Promise\" gathers authentic accounts from visionary women worldwide. Comfort Dondo’s chapter details the foundational promise she made to herself while rebuilding her life in Minnesota—a promise that blossomed into Phumulani: Minnesota African Women Against Violence."]],["DIV",{"class":"pt-2 border-t border-slate-100 flex items-center justify-between"},["BUTTON",{"class":"text-xs font-bold text-[#104F57] hover:text-[#0c3e44] f