dence break the intergenerational cycle of gender-based violence in immigrant diaspora communities."]],["DIV",{"class":"pt-2 border-t border-slate-100 flex items-center justify-between"},["BUTTON",{"class":"text-xs font-bold text-[#104F57] hover:text-[#0c3e44] flex items-center gap-1 cursor-pointer"},["SPAN",{},"Read Excerpts & Details"],["svg",{"xmlns":"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg","width":"24","height":"24","viewBox":"0 0 24 24","fill":"none","stroke":"currentColor","stroke-width":"2","stroke-linecap":"round","stroke-linejoin":"round","class":"lucide lucide-chevron-right w-3.5 h-3.5","aria-hidden":"true"},["path",{"d":"m9 18 6-6-6-6"}]]],["SPAN",{"class":"text-[11px] text-slate-400"},"By Comfort Dondo"]]]]]],["DIV",{"class":"bg-[#E8F3F1]/70 rounded-2xl border border-teal-200/80 p-6 sm:p-8 grid grid-cols-1 lg:grid-cols-12 gap-8 items-center"},["DIV",{"class":"lg:col-span-7 rounded-xl overflow-hidden shadow-lg border border-teal-200 bg-white"},["IMG",{"__playwright_current_src__":"http://localhost:3000/images/homepage/community-hero.svg","alt":"Comfort Dondo facilitating authentic community healing circle in Brooklyn Park","class":"w-full h-auto object-cover","loading":"lazy","referrerpolicy":"no-referrer","src":"/images/homepage/community-hero.svg"}]],["DIV",{"class":"lg:col-span-5 space-y-4"},["SPAN",{"class":"text-[11px] font-bold text-[#104F57] bg-white border border-teal-200 px-3 py-1 rounded-full uppercase tracking-wider"},"Cultural Healing Methodology"],["H3",{"class":"font-serif text-2xl font-bold text-slate-900"},"The Tea Healing Circle Model"],["P",{"class":"text-xs sm:text-sm text-slate-700 leading-relaxed"},"Originated by Comfort Dondo at Phumulani, weekly Tea Healing Circles create a confidential sanctuary where African immigrant women gather to drink spiced tea, decompress from chronic survival stress, and share experiences without judgment."],["DIV",{"class":"p-3 bg-white/80 rounded-xl border border-teal-200/80 text-xs text-slate-600 space-y-1"},["DIV"